  "label": "Medical diagnosis trends and awareness",
  "description": "The increasing recognition and diagnosis of gluten-related disorders (like celiac disease and non-celiac gluten sensitivity) in recent decades is due to improved diagnostic tools, greater public awareness, and increased medical research. This is not a recent 'epidemic' caused by bread consumption, but rather a result of better understanding and access to healthcare.",
